# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-5 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-5 throughout: B5 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after B5's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# B5: build tp4-serve-5 and smoke the PRODUCTION configuration: c2-packed-tp4, the traffic profile, audits ON, the tail caps ON. This
# image carries the capture plug seal fix (the seal no longer plugs the reserve hole: v186 ran out of memory in 'stage capture plug
# seal') and ttexalens for the stall watch's triage (the build installs the pinned tt-metal triage requirements and fails unless
# ttexalens imports). The production profile sets neither the plug nor the stall watch, so this job is B4's configuration on the new image.
# The test list is B4's, unchanged and in its order: T1's SS list, concurrent4_solo, then the two coding-text concurrency tests.
# READ the log: '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' and no UNQUALIFIED line; no late prefill program; c2_smoke_check clean with
# audit_mismatches 0; no watchdog or replay-deadline exit; every concurrent user at 800 tokens; every concurrent4 hash equal to its
# concurrent4_solo run; speed within 5% of v166 (coding 35.84, long_real_text 34.59, concurrent4 15.79, concurrent4_steady 17.24 tok/s).
# Also read the build's '[TRIAGE-CHECK]' line: ttexalens must be present (the Dockerfile layer fails the build otherwise).
# Duration (estimate): 45 min. Stop rule: a hang or a refusal on this configuration stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-5
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
